(footprint "Supercap_Prismatic_13.0x7.0mm_L28.5mm_P10.00mm_Horizontal"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Prismatic (rectangular can) EDLC supercapacitor module mounted HORIZONTALLY (leads bent 90 deg). Can axis parallel to the board, 7.0 mm tall above whatever it sits on. Cross-section is OBROUND, not rectangular - 13.0 mm across x 7.0 mm thick with 3.5 mm radius sides (two ~6.3 mm cells side by side under shrink wrap, per the CHP series end-view drawings), so it rests on a ~6.0 mm wide flat. Two radial leads on 10.00 mm pitch exit the end face and bend down to the pads; 2.5 mm is allowed between pad centre and the can's near face for the bend. Drawn for CDA/Zhifengwei CHP5R5L205R-TWQ (2.0 F, 5.5 V; ESR 190 mohm @1 kHz / ~380 mohm DC). Pad 1 = POSITIVE. 3D model: hardware/3dmodels/Supercap_Prismatic_13.0x7.0mm_L28.5mm_P10.00mm_Horizontal.step (obround blue sleeve + steel bent leads, colour carried in the STEP). *** DELIBERATELY NO COURTYARD OVER THE BODY *** - the can is glued down OVER other components, so the only keep-out is a small courtyard around the two legs. The body outline is on F.Fab as documentation only and generates no DRC. MECHANICAL: parts under the can must clear its underside (set by your standoff/glue line); parts under the 2.5 mm lead bend must stay below ~3 mm, since the lead descends there from the can's 3.5 mm mid-height to the board. Vertical variant of the same part: Supercap_Prismatic_13.0x7.0mm_H28.5mm_P10.00mm. Datasheet: CDA CHP(5.5V) Series, spec date 2022-05-17.")
	(tags "supercapacitor EDLC prismatic horizontal lay-down bent-lead glued no-keepout radial tht polarised CHP")
